---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { contactEmail, privacyLastUpdated, siteName } from "../site.config";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy policy" width="tutorial" ads={false}>
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <p>Last updated: {privacyLastUpdated}</p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    {siteName} is a free reference website. You can contact us about this policy
    at <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>The calculator</h2>
  <p>
    Everything the calculator works out is worked out in your browser. What you
    type into it is never sent anywhere and never saved, not even in your
    browser. The site is a reference tool for health professionals, not advice
    about any individual.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    The site shows ads from Google AdSense. The ads are non-personalised: they
    are chosen from the content of the page, not from anything known about you.
    Google still uses cookies or similar storage on your device for frequency
    capping, fraud prevention and aggregate reporting, and it receives your IP
    address when your browser requests an ad. Read <a
      href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites"
      >how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    We use Cloudflare Web Analytics to count page views, referring sites and
    visitors' countries. It uses no cookies and doesn't track you across other
    sites.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>
    The site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. Cloudflare processes your IP address
    and details of each request, such as the page asked for and your browser
    type, to deliver the site and protect it from abuse.
  </p>

  <h2>Storage on your device</h2>
  <p>
    The site itself stores one item in your browser's <code>localStorage</code>: a
    note that you dismissed the privacy notice, so it isn't shown again. It is
    not a cookie and is never sent to us. Clearing your browser's site data
    removes it.
  </p>

  <h2>What we don't do</h2>
  <p>
    There are no accounts, forms or sign-ups, and no personalised ads. We don't
    sell or share personal information.
  </p>

  <h2>Overseas</h2>
  <p>
    Google and Cloudflare may process data outside Australia and New Zealand,
    including in the United States. This is disclosed under Australian Privacy
    Principle 8 and New Zealand Information Privacy Principle 12.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    We don't hold any personal information about you. If you have a question
    about privacy, email <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
    If you want to make a complaint, you can contact the <a
      href="https://www.oaic.gov.au/"
      >Office of the Australian Information Commissioner</a
    > (Australia) or the <a href="https://www.privacy.org.nz/"
      >Office of the Privacy Commissioner</a
    > (New Zealand).
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    The date at the top of this page shows when the policy last changed. When
    something material changes, such as a new third party, new data being
    collected or a move to personalised ads, we show the privacy notice again
    to every visitor.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
